      <h1>China Battery Production: The 2024-2025 Time Series</h1>
      <p class="muted">Battery Market Intelligence · MIIT data · Last reviewed 2026-09-16</p>

      <div class="box">
        <strong>Direct answer:</strong> China's lithium-ion battery production reached <strong>1,170 GWh in
        2024</strong> — up <strong>24% year-on-year</strong>, split between <strong>826 GWh of power batteries</strong>
        and <strong>260 GWh of storage-grade cells</strong>. For 2025, output is on track to pass
        <strong>1,500 GWh (+28%)</strong>, with storage accelerating toward <strong>550 GWh</strong> — roughly
        doubling in a year.
      </div>

      <h2>The production time series (MIIT)</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Period</th><th>Total</th><th>Power batteries</th><th>Storage-grade</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>2024</td><td><strong>1,170 GWh</strong> (+24% YoY)</td><td>826 GWh</td><td>260 GWh</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2025 (projected)</td><td><strong>&gt;1,500 GWh</strong> (+28%)</td><td>—</td><td>~550 GWh</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="muted">Source: Ministry of Industry and Information Technology (MIIT), industry reporting.</p>

      <h2>Our calculation</h2>
      <div class="box">
        <p><strong>The storage surge:</strong> 260 GWh (2024) to ~550 GWh (2025) is roughly
        <strong>+112% in one year</strong> — storage is now the fastest layer of Chinese production, compounding
        far faster than the ~24–28% overall growth. Power batteries were about <strong>71% of 2024 output</strong>
        (826 ÷ 1,170); the storage share is rising quickly.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>What the numbers mean</h2>
      <p>
        The production series mirrors the market structure: <strong>power batteries carry the volume</strong>, but
        <strong>storage carries the growth</strong> — the same two-engine shape as the
        <a href="/battery-demand-forecast/">demand forecast</a>. Output growing at ~25% per year means roughly
        <strong>a decade's tripling every five years</strong> of the base, which is why capacity keeps racing
        demand (see <a href="/china-lithium-industry/">China's lithium industry</a>).
      </p>

      <h2>The Author's Take</h2>
      <div class="box">
        <p><strong>My read:</strong> China's production series is best read as two growth rates, not one total —
        power batteries compounding at ~25%, storage at over 100% — and the storage rate is the number that will
        reshape the industry's structure this decade.</p>
        <p><strong>Why:</strong> The total masks the shift. Storage doubling annually changes the mix within a few
        years — exactly the structural change that capacity plans, price forecasts and export structures must be
        built around, not just observed.</p>
        <p class="muted"><em>My editorial view, not investment or purchasing advice.</em></p>
      </div>

